1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,431
Welcome to TrainMe, the training tracker for athletes and gym-goers.

2
00:00:04,481 --> 00:00:16,999
In the next few minutes we will walk through the member experience on mobile and web, from sign-up to logging every ball of a bowling session, charts, history and comparisons, and then the admin console that runs the platform.

3
00:00:18,449 --> 00:00:20,757
TrainMe is one platform with three apps.

4
00:00:20,807 --> 00:00:25,003
The mobile app is where athletes log sessions live, even without signal.

5
00:00:25,053 --> 00:00:29,308
The web app gives a big-screen view of progress, history and comparisons.

6
00:00:29,358 --> 00:00:35,559
And the admin console is where the team curates the activity catalog, supports users and manages releases.

7
00:00:36,708 --> 00:00:38,060
Getting started is quick.

8
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:41,422
A new member can sign up with one tap using Apple or Google.

9
00:00:41,472 --> 00:00:46,970
Or they enter their name, email and a password, and a live strength meter guides them as they type.

10
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:53,079
Consent to the terms and privacy policy is explicit, and the create account button stays clear and prominent.

11
00:00:54,229 --> 00:00:56,495
Next, onboarding personalises the app.

12
00:00:56,545 --> 00:01:02,469
The member picks what they train, here cricket and gym, then their role in cricket, a fast bowler.

13
00:01:02,519 --> 00:01:05,151
Roles only appear for sports that have them.

14
00:01:05,201 --> 00:01:07,894
Tennis and badminton, for example, have none.

15
00:01:07,944 --> 00:01:13,319
Finally they choose metric or imperial units, and TrainMe recommends the right templates.

16
00:01:14,469 --> 00:01:18,230
Returning members log in in a second with Face ID or a passkey.

17
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:25,307
Email and password, and Apple or Google, are always available, with a forgot-password link right where you expect it.

18
00:01:25,357 --> 00:01:33,896
Behind the scenes, TrainMe uses the industry-standard OpenID Connect flow with PKCE, and short-lived tokens are stored securely on the device.

19
00:01:35,046 --> 00:01:37,855
On a laptop, the same account opens the web app.

20
00:01:37,905 --> 00:01:43,096
The sign-in page is designed to be inviting, with a preview of what you will see inside.

21
00:01:43,146 --> 00:01:51,732
Members can use a passkey, Google, Apple or email, and choose to stay signed in on trusted devices, which they can review and revoke at any time.

22
00:01:52,882 --> 00:01:55,482
The home screen shows training at a glance.

23
00:01:55,532 --> 00:02:04,293
A streak counter keeps motivation high, the weekly ring shows progress towards the goal, and every personal tracker has a one-tap start button.

24
00:02:04,343 --> 00:02:09,900
New personal bests, like a top speed of 138 kilometres per hour, are celebrated right here.

25
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:14,003
To add something new, members explore the catalog.

26
00:02:14,053 --> 00:02:20,252
Search is forgiving of typos and synonyms, so searching yorker finds the right bowling drills instantly.

27
00:02:20,302 --> 00:02:28,182
You can also browse the tree, from sports to cricket, bowling and fast bowler, and filter by sport, role, equipment or muscle group.

28
00:02:29,332 --> 00:02:40,407
The Fast Bowler template shows exactly what will be tracked: speed, line and length, and an attempted and accurate pair for every skill, yorker, seam, bouncer, swing and slower ball.

29
00:02:40,457 --> 00:02:42,730
One tap adds it as a personal tracker.

30
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:44,747
Here it is named My Fast Bowling.

31
00:02:45,897 --> 00:02:49,977
Every athlete trains differently, so trackers are fully customisable.

32
00:02:50,027 --> 00:02:53,687
Here the bowler adds a new yes or no field called slower ball.

33
00:02:53,737 --> 00:02:57,817
Fields can be conditional, appearing only when another answer is yes.

34
00:02:57,867 --> 00:03:03,801
And TrainMe can automatically create a ratio metric, slower-ball rate, so it shows up in the charts.

35
00:03:03,851 --> 00:03:05,836
The shared template never changes.

36
00:03:06,986 --> 00:03:08,321
Now the session begins.

37
00:03:08,371 --> 00:03:14,881
The live screen shows a timer and an over and ball counter, because deliveries are grouped into overs of six.

38
00:03:14,931 --> 00:03:21,322
Live stats, like balls bowled, yorker accuracy so far and average speed, update instantly after every ball.

39
00:03:21,372 --> 00:03:24,752
The sync indicator shows the session is safely backed up.

40
00:03:25,903 --> 00:03:27,489
Logging a ball takes seconds.

41
00:03:27,539 --> 00:03:32,005
Nudge the speed with the stepper, tap the line on the pitch and pick the length.

42
00:03:32,055 --> 00:03:36,125
Toggle yorker attempted, and only then does the accurate question appear.

43
00:03:36,175 --> 00:03:40,527
That is a conditional field, so the form stays short and the data stays clean.

44
00:03:40,577 --> 00:03:44,026
The ball is saved on the phone instantly, even with no signal.

45
00:03:45,176 --> 00:03:47,943
Cricket grounds and gyms often have poor signal.

46
00:03:47,993 --> 00:03:54,221
TrainMe saves every ball on the device first, so nothing is lost if the network drops or the app is closed.

47
00:03:54,271 --> 00:04:00,030
Every three to five minutes, and whenever the connection returns, a checkpoint syncs the new balls.

48
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:04,606
Each ball has its own ID, so even if a sync is retried, nothing is duplicated.

49
00:04:05,756 --> 00:04:14,191
When the bowler taps end session, the app sends any remaining balls, and the server confirms that all fifty arrived before marking the session complete.

50
00:04:14,241 --> 00:04:23,904
The summary shows each skill as a ratio with its counts: yorkers twelve out of eighteen, seam twenty-three out of thirty, bouncers five out of eight, and just three no-balls.

51
00:04:23,954 --> 00:04:27,198
Notes can be added, and new personal bests are highlighted.

52
00:04:28,348 --> 00:04:32,003
On the web app, the progress page turns sessions into insight.

53
00:04:32,053 --> 00:04:34,692
Switch between day, week and month instantly.

54
00:04:34,742 --> 00:04:45,509
Ratio charts are calculated correctly across sessions, by adding up the accurate and attempted counts, and the tooltip shows both: sixty-six point seven percent, twelve of eighteen.

55
00:04:45,559 --> 00:04:50,410
Smaller charts track average speed trending up and the no-ball rate trending down.

56
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:54,031
The sessions page keeps the full history.

57
00:04:54,081 --> 00:05:03,010
Filter by date range, search your notes, for example new run-up, or find sessions by a metric, such as yorker accuracy of seventy percent or more.

58
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:08,053
Results come back in milliseconds, even with thousands of users logging every day.

59
00:05:08,103 --> 00:05:11,189
Tick a few sessions, and compare them side by side.

60
00:05:12,339 --> 00:05:14,733
The compare view puts sessions side by side.

61
00:05:14,783 --> 00:05:21,010
Grouped bars show every skill metric for the nineteenth of September, the twenty-sixth, and the third of October.

62
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:26,176
The speed-by-over chart shows the bowler is now faster and more consistent through the spell.

63
00:05:26,226 --> 00:05:34,453
And the delta panel spells it out: yorker accuracy up sixteen points, average speed up three point four, and two fewer no-balls since the new run-up.

64
00:05:35,603 --> 00:05:38,847
The same engine works for every sport and for the gym.

65
00:05:38,897 --> 00:05:42,569
Here is a push day: each set records reps, weight and effort.

66
00:05:42,619 --> 00:05:46,656
Mark a set as taken to failure, and an assisted reps field appears.

67
00:05:46,706 --> 00:05:58,553
TrainMe calculates training volume and an estimated one-rep max automatically, and the exercises come from a shared library organised by muscle group: chest, back, shoulders, arms, legs and core.

68
00:05:59,703 --> 00:06:01,169
TrainMe is free to start.

69
00:06:01,219 --> 00:06:04,322
The plans page compares Free, Pro and Elite clearly.

70
00:06:04,372 --> 00:06:10,326
Pro unlocks unlimited trackers, custom parameters and full history, with a fourteen-day free trial.

71
00:06:10,376 --> 00:06:16,754
Checkout is handled by the payment provider or the app store, so card details are never stored by TrainMe.

72
00:06:17,904 --> 00:06:18,927
Now the team side.

73
00:06:18,977 --> 00:06:22,919
The admin console is a separate app with its own role-based access.

74
00:06:22,969 --> 00:06:31,677
Every admin must complete multi-factor authentication, here with a six-digit code, and every admin action is written to a tamper-evident audit log.

75
00:06:32,827 --> 00:06:43,436
The overview shows the platform at a glance: over ten thousand registered users, nearly seven thousand active today, twenty-one thousand sessions, and the Pro conversion rate.

76
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:47,578
A live chart shows sessions by hour, peaking after evening training.

77
00:06:47,628 --> 00:06:56,228
The system health panel compares key numbers with their targets: API latency, search response time, sync lag and error rate, all in the green.

78
00:06:57,378 --> 00:07:02,913
The catalog manager is where curators add sports, drills and exercises without writing code.

79
00:07:02,963 --> 00:07:07,587
They browse the tree, then edit an activity's fields, conditions and metrics.

80
00:07:07,637 --> 00:07:11,594
Here a new field, wide reason, appears only when a ball is a wide.

81
00:07:11,644 --> 00:07:14,872
The metric builder defines yorker accuracy as a ratio.

82
00:07:14,922 --> 00:07:19,971
Before publishing version three, TrainMe validates everything and shows the changes.

83
00:07:20,021 --> 00:07:24,403
Existing trackers stay on version two until each user chooses to upgrade.

84
00:07:25,553 --> 00:07:31,505
For support, admins can find a user and see what they need to help, while personal data stays masked.

85
00:07:31,555 --> 00:07:38,103
The profile shows the plan and renewal date, signed-in devices, and sync status, including the last checkpoint.

86
00:07:38,153 --> 00:07:41,966
Health and training data is hidden unless the user gives consent.

87
00:07:42,016 --> 00:07:48,503
Safe actions like revoking sessions or resending a verification email are one click away, and each is audited.

88
00:07:49,653 --> 00:07:51,674
New features are rolled out safely.

89
00:07:51,724 --> 00:07:58,420
Feature flags turn them on for a percentage of users, for example the new chart design for ten percent of members.

90
00:07:58,470 --> 00:08:04,988
Releases go out as canaries: a small share of traffic first, with automatic rollback if errors or latency rise.

91
00:08:05,038 --> 00:08:07,710
And every change is recorded in the audit log.

92
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:23,217
That's TrainMe: intuitive sign-up and login, live ball-by-ball logging that works offline, clear charts, searchable history and side-by-side comparisons, plus an admin console that manages the catalog, users and releases without code.

93
00:08:23,267 --> 00:08:24,633
Thank you for watching.
